{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id134263913"}, "name":{"label":"Tom Cassidy"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-24T03:03:57-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1622821959"}, "title":{"label":"Clean. Easy. Beautiful. Functional."}, "content":{"label":"This is by a country mile the best personal productivity app I've had the joy to use. I use Trello for all project related things and I've played with Evernote, and Omnifocus and Wunderlist and so on. Pretty much all of the big ones. Especially with a GTD focus. \n\nBut none have really come close to allowing me to work the way I want. What's terrific about Things3 is the sheer elegance of the beast. It's just beautiful. And not just 'in the way it looks' kind of beautiful.\n\nNo. Much more like 'In the way you first discovered something really neat; like the first time you moved to a mac from windows, or the first time you unboxed an iPhone, or first used Gmail after all the horrible email services at the time. \n\nIt's a work of art. Loving it big time. And I'm using it for a much more effective productivity system based on a combination of Agile Results by JD Meier with some influence from GTD. \n\nPAY THE MONEY.\n\nGet Things3.\n\nBecause it just works....", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id448439773"}, "name":{"label":"Spikes mike"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-24T00:53:16-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1622704829"}, "title":{"label":"Exceptional"}, "content":{"label":"Has been difficult to organize all aspects of a busy life efficiently without Things 2. Things 3 has just made it better. Much better actually. It's such fun to use as well.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id28716017"}, "name":{"label":"wanderlust167"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2017-05-24T00:45:59-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.0.2"}, "id":{"label":"1622698058"}, "title":{"label":"So good I switched"}, "content":{"label":"I was using 2Do which I found had every permutation that you could think of for any way of working. But the niggle for me was that it took too many inputs to place a new task that I found it sometimes disrupted my train of thought. Also, since the last update it was slower to open and present the initial input screen. \nThings is extremely quick to present the first screen and then adding tasks is a doddle. It may not have all the features that 2Do has, like location alerts, but I can live with that and just use the reminders app if needed. \nThe design is flawless and helps focus my mind on what I need to do rather than trying to pick out the detail from unnecessary information. \nOverall highly recommended.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=904237743&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
